<div class="pd-chat-documentation">
	<section id="overview">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Overview</h2>
		<p><code>PDChat</code> is a chat/messaging UI component with message bubbles and input.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Parameters</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Messages</code></td><td><code>List&lt;ChatMessage&gt;</code></td><td>Messages to display</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnSend</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;string&gt;</code></td><td>Fired when user sends message</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Icons</code></td><td><code>PDChatIcons</code></td><td>The CSS classes of the header and toolbar icons. Font Awesome by default. See <a href="#icons-and-theming">Icons and theming</a>.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>
	<section id="conversation-history">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Conversation history</h2>
		<p>
			A host that can store conversations implements <code>IChatConversationService</code> and passes it
			as <code>ConversationService</code>. That is what makes a conversation list, conversation tabs and
			their toolbar available. A host that passes nothing gets exactly the chat described above &mdash;
			no conversation UI, and no code path that could show it.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>SupportsSemanticSearch</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>Whether this store can match on meaning as well as wording. Defaults to <code>false</code>; the semantic option is hidden rather than disabled when it is.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ListAsync</code></td><td><code>Task&lt;ChatConversationPage&gt;</code></td><td>The conversations matching a <code>ChatConversationQuery</code>. Matching nothing returns <code>ChatConversationPage.Empty</code>, not an error.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>GetMessagesAsync</code></td><td><code>Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;ChatMessage&gt;&gt;</code></td><td>One conversation's transcript, oldest first. Separate from the list so that listing 200 conversations does not fetch 200 transcripts.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>CreateAsync</code></td><td><code>Task&lt;ChatConversation&gt;</code></td><td>A new, empty conversation. Call it lazily &mdash; on the first message, not when the user clicks <em>new</em>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>RenameAsync</code></td><td><code>Task</code></td><td>Sets a title. Renaming to blank titles it as blank; it does not return it to the untitled state.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ArchiveAsync</code> / <code>UnarchiveAsync</code></td><td><code>Task</code></td><td>Hides a conversation from a list that has not asked for archived ones, and puts it back.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			<strong>There is no <code>DeleteAsync</code>, and there will not be one.</strong> A transcript is a
			record of what an assistant told somebody, so a conversation is archived and never removed. The
			guarantee is the absence of the method rather than a UI that hides a button &mdash; a UI-only
			guarantee lasts until the next person adds a convenience call.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Scoping results to the current user is the implementer's job.</strong> The component has no
			notion of who is signed in and will render whatever it is handed, without error. An implementation
			that returns unscoped rows will show one user another user's transcripts.
		</p>
		<p>
			<code>ChatConversationQuery</code> carries <code>SearchText</code> (test it with
			<code>HasSearchText</code>, which ignores whitespace), <code>SearchMode</code>, an
			<code>IncludeArchived</code> that defaults to <strong>false</strong>, and
			<code>Skip</code>/<code>Take</code>. On the returned <code>ChatConversationPage</code>,
			<code>HasMore</code> is stated by the implementer rather than inferred from a short page, and
			<code>TotalCount</code> is nullable: <code>null</code> means <em>not counted</em>, which is
			deliberately distinct from <code>0</code>, meaning <em>counted, and there are none</em>.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section id="conversation-fullscreen">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Full-screen conversation UI</h2>
		<p>
			Supplying <code>ConversationService</code> is what turns full-screen into a multi-conversation
			workspace. <strong>Try it on this page:</strong> open the chat, click the maximise button, then pick
			a conversation from the sidebar. The demo is backed by an in-memory
			<code>DemoChatConversationService</code> over the same <code>DumbChatService</code> that holds the
			transcripts, seeded with a few conversations including an archived one.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Sidebar</strong> &mdash; conversations newest-first, with search that is debounced and
				cancellable so a superseded query cannot overwrite a newer result. The semantic/keyword toggle is
				<em>hidden</em> rather than greyed when the store has no embedding model, which is why you will not
				see it here.</li>
			<li><strong>Tabs</strong> &mdash; one per <em>open</em> conversation. Opening one already open selects
				its tab rather than duplicating it. Closing a tab neither archives nor deletes.</li>
			<li><strong>Unread markers</strong> &mdash; send a message, switch to another tab, and wait: the reply
				marks the tab it belongs to and does not drag you back to it.</li>
			<li><strong>Include archived</strong> &mdash; unchecked by default. Tick it to reveal the seeded
				archived conversation.</li>
			<li><strong>Archive and un-archive</strong> &mdash; archiving closes the tab and drops the conversation
				out of the default list. To get it back: tick <em>Include archived</em>, open it, and use
				<em>Un-archive</em> in the toolbar. Opening an archived conversation does <em>not</em> silently
				un-archive it, so you can read one without dragging it back into the list; and un-archiving leaves it
				open, because you have just said you want it. The control is hidden, not greyed, when the
				conversation is not archived. There is no delete, anywhere.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			None of this appears in the docked, minimised or toast modes: the feature deliberately leaves the chat
			most users see most of the time completely unchanged.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section id="toasts">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Toast notifications</h2>
		<p>
			<code>PDChat</code> can double as a toast surface. When a message arrives while the chat is
			<em>closed</em> &mdash; minimized to its button, or fully hidden when
			<code>MinimizedButtonPosition</code> is <code>None</code> (a headless toast) &mdash; the message
			animates into view. It stays for a configurable time and then, if auto-dismiss is enabled,
			animates out again.
		</p>
		<p>
			Multiple toasts <strong>stack</strong> (oldest at the top, newest at the bottom) and each runs
			its own independent dismiss timer, so a longer-lived toast can outlast a later, shorter one.
			While more than one toast is present, a dismissing toast leaves via a fixed de-stack animation;
			the last remaining toast uses its own configured exit animation. Clicking a toast opens the
			chat; hovering pauses its dismiss timer.
		</p>
		<p>
			Defaults are configured on <code>IChatService</code> via the <code>Toast*</code> members and can
			be overridden per message with <code>ChatMessage.ToastOptions</code> (any unset override falls
			back to the service default).
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>IChatService member</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>ToastEnabled</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Master switch (supersedes <code>ShowLastMessage</code>).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastEntryAnimation</code></td><td><code>PDChatToastAnimation</code></td><td><code>Grow</code></td><td>Animation used when a toast appears.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastExitAnimation</code></td><td><code>PDChatToastAnimation</code></td><td><code>Shrink</code></td><td>Animation used when a toast is dismissed.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastAnimationDurationMs</code></td><td><code>double</code></td><td><code>250</code></td><td>Entry / exit transition time in milliseconds.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastAutoDismiss</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether toasts auto-dismiss after the display duration.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastDisplayDurationSeconds</code></td><td><code>double</code></td><td><code>5</code></td><td>Dwell time before auto-dismiss (supersedes <code>ShowLastMessageDurationSeconds</code>).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastShowTitle</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether the message title is shown in the toast.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastMinWidth</code> / <code>ToastMaxWidth</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>200px</code> / <code>300px</code></td><td>Toast width constraints (any CSS length).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastMinHeight</code> / <code>ToastMaxHeight</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>(auto)</td><td>Toast height constraints (any CSS length).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastMaxVisible</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td><code>5</code></td><td>Max toasts shown at once; the oldest is dismissed to make room.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ToastAnchor</code></td><td><code>PDChatButtonPosition</code></td><td><code>BottomRight</code></td><td>Corner the stack anchors to when the button is hidden (otherwise it follows the button).</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p class="text-muted small">
			<code>ShowLastMessage</code> and <code>ShowLastMessageDurationSeconds</code> are obsolete and map onto
			<code>ToastEnabled</code> / <code>ToastDisplayDurationSeconds</code> for backward compatibility.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section id="input-toolbar">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Input toolbar, voice and wake phrase</h2>
		<p>
			A thin toolbar sits above the text box. It holds an agent picker and a model picker (each shown only when
			the service lists two or more), the notification sounds bell (<code>IsMuted</code>), and, when the service
			supplies <code>VoiceEndpoints</code>, a read-aloud speaker and a microphone. Dictated words are typed into
			the text box and sent after a pause unless the user is editing. All of these are configured on
			<code>IChatService</code> and have defaults, so an existing service needs no change.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>IChatService member</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Agents</code> / <code>SelectedAgentId</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;PDChatAgentOption&gt;?</code> / <code>string?</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Who the user is talking to.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AgentPickerAction</code></td><td><code>PDChatPickerAction?</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>An action ending the agent picker after a separator, such as <code>[+] New Assistant</code>. Choosing it runs its <code>OnChosen</code> callback and never changes <code>SelectedAgentId</code>. With an action the picker shows for a single agent too.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Models</code> / <code>SelectedModelId</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;PDChatModelOption&gt;?</code> / <code>string?</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Which model answers.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VoiceEndpoints</code></td><td><code>PDChatVoiceEndpoints?</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Where speech is sent and answers fetched; <code>null</code> hides the voice controls. <code>PDChatVoiceEndpoints.Simulated</code> needs no speech service.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IsReadAloudEnabled</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Reads the answer to each sent message aloud. Independent of the microphone and of notification sounds.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VoiceAutoSendDelay</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan</code></td><td>1 second</td><td>How long after a pause dictation is sent, when the user is not editing.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>WakePhrases</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;string&gt;?</code></td><td><code>null</code> (off)</td><td>Phrases such as "Hey DumbBot" that wake a dormant microphone. Case and punctuation are ignored, and the phrase itself is never typed.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VoiceIdleTimeout</code></td><td><code>TimeSpan</code></td><td>10 seconds</td><td>How long the microphone may hear nothing before it goes dormant. Applies only with wake phrases.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VoiceMode</code></td><td><code>PDChatVoiceMode</code></td><td><code>Hal</code></td><td>The mode the user last chose: <code>Hal</code> listens at once and sends on a pause; <code>Dictate</code> listens only while the text box has focus and never sends by itself; <code>Wake</code> starts dormant and returns there after each exchange (offered only with wake phrases). The picker also has a first choice, "Mic off", that stops listening and releases the microphone without changing this value. Implement it to remember the choice per user.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AnsweringModelName</code> / <code>AnsweringModelDescription</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td><code>null</code> (nothing shown)</td><td>The model that answered the latest turn, shown as an "answered by" badge after the model picker, with the description as its tooltip.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IsImageInputOffered</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Offers images: Ctrl+V paste, drag and drop, an attach button and a screenshot button (this tab only). Images stack, numbered, above the text box (at most five), and go in <code>ChatMessage.Images</code>, shown full width in the message.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ImageInputBlockedReason</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>When set, the images stay but Send is disabled and this is shown, for example because the selected model cannot take images.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			The microphone is one split control: the button starts and stops listening, and the select beside it picks
			the mode. The button shows the mode as its icon (the HAL eye, a microphone, or an ear) and the state through
			its colour and motion: listening, editing, thinking, speaking, dormant or paused. Its title says both in words.
			In <code>Hal</code> and <code>Wake</code>, clicking in the text box switches to manual: dictation keeps
			streaming into the box, Send submits, and the next pause sends again. A message's
			<code>SpokenMessage</code>, when set, is read aloud in place of the message, which is displayed unchanged; an
			empty value reads nothing.
		</p>
		<p>
			With wake phrases set, Voice Mode goes <code>Dormant</code> after the idle timeout (never while the user is
			editing or a send is pending). While dormant nothing is typed or sent until a wake phrase is heard; the words
			after it are typed as usual. The microphone keeps streaming to the speech service while dormant, since it
			must hear the phrase, so tell your users that a dormant microphone is still listening. Try it with the
			<strong>Voice and Assistant</strong> settings on this page: the simulated microphone starts every other
			utterance with "Hey DumbBot".
		</p>
		<p>
			Narrower than about 860px, the toolbar uses two rows: the pickers, then the other controls on the left with
			Send on the right. Narrower than 420px, as when docked to a corner, the picker labels and the word Send are
			hidden; each control keeps its tooltip.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section id="icons-and-theming">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Icons and theming</h2>
		<p>
			The header and toolbar buttons use Font Awesome icons, which the library already needs. Each icon is a CSS
			class on <code>PDChatIcons</code>, passed as the <code>Icons</code> parameter, so a host can use another
			icon set or a Font Awesome Pro style, for example
			<code>Icons="@@(new() { Send = "bi bi-send", Attach = "bi bi-paperclip" })"</code>. An empty class shows
			no icon.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>PDChatIcons property</th><th>Default</th><th>Used for</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Agent</code></td><td><code>fas fa-robot</code></td><td>The agent picker, for an agent with no image of its own</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Model</code></td><td><code>fas fa-microchip</code></td><td>The model picker</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>SoundsOn</code> / <code>SoundsOff</code></td><td><code>fas fa-bell</code> / <code>fas fa-bell-slash</code></td><td>Notification sounds</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ReadAloudOn</code> / <code>ReadAloudOff</code></td><td><code>fas fa-volume-up</code> / <code>fas fa-volume-mute</code></td><td>Read answers aloud</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Dictate</code> / <code>Wake</code></td><td><code>fas fa-microphone</code> / <code>fas fa-assistive-listening-systems</code></td><td>The microphone in Dictate and wake phrase modes. HAL shows its eye.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>VoiceStarting</code> / <code>VoicePaused</code></td><td><code>fas fa-circle-notch fa-spin</code> / <code>fas fa-pause</code></td><td>The microphone while it opens, and the badge on it while dictation is paused</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Attach</code> / <code>Screenshot</code></td><td><code>fas fa-paperclip</code> / <code>fas fa-camera</code></td><td>The image buttons</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Send</code></td><td><code>fas fa-paper-plane</code></td><td>Send</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Clear</code></td><td><code>fas fa-trash-alt</code></td><td>Clear chat, in the header</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Pin</code></td><td><code>fas fa-thumbtack</code></td><td>Docks a corner chat to the side, and shows pressed while docked, when it unpins</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>FullScreen</code> / <code>Restore</code></td><td><code>fas fa-expand</code> / <code>fas fa-compress</code></td><td>Full screen, and leaving it</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Minimize</code></td><td><code>fas fa-minus</code></td><td>Minimise</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			Colours and sizes are CSS variables. Each is read where it is used, so a host can set it on
			<code>:root</code>, on a theme class or on <code>.pdchat-container</code>, and anything left unset keeps its
			default. For example, <code>body.theme-lime { --pd-chat-send-color: #112100; }</code> gives Send dark text on
			a light accent.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-accent</code></td><td><code>--accent</code>, then <code>--bs-primary</code></td><td>The header, Send and the toolbar's focus rings</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-header-color</code></td><td><code>#fff</code></td><td>Header text and buttons</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-font-family</code></td><td><code>Arial, sans-serif</code></td><td>The chat's font</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-toolbar-bg</code> / <code>-border</code></td><td><code>--pd-chat-secondary-bg</code> / <code>--pd-chat-border</code></td><td>The toolbar and the strip around the text box</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-toolbar-padding</code> / <code>-gap</code> / <code>-font-size</code></td><td><code>5px 8px</code> / <code>6px</code> / <code>0.8125rem</code></td><td>Toolbar spacing and text size</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-control-height</code> / <code>-radius</code></td><td><code>28px</code> / <code>6px</code></td><td>Every picker, button and Send</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-control-bg</code> / <code>-color</code> / <code>-border</code></td><td><code>--pd-chat-bg</code> / <code>--pd-chat-color</code> / <code>--pd-chat-border</code></td><td>The picker fields</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-control-hover-bg</code></td><td><code>rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.14)</code></td><td>Any control under the pointer</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-control-active-color</code> / <code>-active-bg</code></td><td><code>--pd-chat-color</code> / <code>rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.22)</code></td><td>A toggle that is on, such as read aloud</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-icon-color</code> / <code>-size</code></td><td><code>--pd-chat-muted-color</code> / <code>0.95rem</code></td><td>Toolbar icons</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-badge-bg</code> / <code>-color</code></td><td><code>rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.16)</code> / <code>--pd-chat-muted-color</code></td><td>The "answered by" badge</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-send-bg</code> / <code>-color</code> / <code>-radius</code></td><td><code>--pd-chat-accent</code> / <code>#fff</code> / <code>--pd-chat-control-radius</code></td><td>Send</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-voice-listening</code></td><td><code>#dc3545</code></td><td>The microphone while listening, and its outline while dormant</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-voice-thinking</code> / <code>-speaking</code> / <code>-editing</code></td><td><code>#6c757d</code> / <code>#0d6efd</code> / <code>#ffc107</code></td><td>The microphone in the other states</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-chat-voice-hal-bg</code></td><td><code>#111</code></td><td>The microphone behind the HAL eye</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>
</div>
